um","gloss":"first-person plural suffix"}],"gloss":"we ask"},{"surface":"தெற்றெனப்","parts":[{"text":"தெற்றெனப்","lemma":"தெற்றெனப்","gloss":"clearly"}],"gloss":"clearly","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பசிப்பிணி","parts":[{"text":"பசி","lemma":"paci","gloss":"hunger"},{"text":"பிணி","lemma":"piṇi","gloss":"disease"}],"gloss":"disease of hunger"},{"surface":"மருத்துவன்","parts":[{"text":"மருத்துவன்","lemma":"maruttuvaṉ","gloss":"doctor"}],"gloss":"doctor"},{"surface":"இல்லம்","parts":[{"text":"இல்லம்","lemma":"illam","gloss":"house"}],"gloss":"house"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அணித்தோ","parts":[{"text":"அணித்து","lemma":"aṇittu","gloss":"near"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ō","gloss":"interrogative suffix"}],"gloss":"is it near?"},{"surface":"சேய்த்தோ","parts":[{"text":"சேய்த்து","lemma":"cēyttu","gloss":"far"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ō","gloss":"interrogative suffix"}],"gloss":"is it far?"},{"surface":"கூறுமின்","parts":[{"text":"கூறு","lemma":"kūṟu","gloss":"tell"},{"text":"மின்","lemma":"miṉ","gloss":"plural imperative suffix"}],"gloss":"tell!"},{"surface":"எமக்கே","parts":[{"text":"எமக்கே","lemma":"எமக்கே","gloss":"to us indeed"}],"gloss":"to us indeed","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"May Paṇṇaṉ live even the days that I am to live! / Let bards see! The distress of this man's family, / like the chirping of birds on a fertile fruit-bearing tree, / the sound of eating itself is heard. / Looking towards the place where the unfailing cloud rains, / taking their eggs and reaching the dry high ground, / resembling the fine row of small, tiny ants, / those with hands holding cooked rice moving in distinct groups, / we see the children of his large family, and having seen, / again and again we ask clearly: / \"The house of the doctor who cures the disease of hunger, / is it near or is it far? Tell us!\"","translation":"May Paṇṇaṉ live for all the days that I am destined to live! Let bards look upon the distress of this bard's family. Like the chirping of birds gathered on a fertile, fruit-bearing tree, the loud sound of eating is heard there. Just as tiny ants, sensing rain from the unfailing clouds, carry their eggs in a fine line to the dry high ground, children of large families are seen moving in distinct groups, hands filled with cooked rice. Seeing them, we ask again and again, to be absolutely sure: 'The house of the doctor who cures the disease of hunger—is it near or is it far? Tell us!'","modern":"நான் வாழும் நாட்களையும் சேர்த்துப் பண்ணன் வாழட்டும்! பாணர்களே, இவனுடைய சுற்றத்தாரின் வறுமையைக் காணுங்கள். செழுமையான பழ மரத்தில் பறவைகள் ஒலிப்பது போல, அங்கே உணவு உண்ணும் ஓசை கேட்கிறது. பொய்க்காத மேகம் பொழியும் இடத்தை நோக்கி, முட்டைகளைச் சுமந்து கொண்டு மேட்டு நிலத்திற்குச் செல்லும் சிறிய, நுட்பமான எறும்புகளின் வரிசையைப் போல, கைகளில் சோற்றுடன் பெருங்கூட்டமாகச் செல்லும் சிறுவர்களைக் காண்கிறோம். அவர்களைக் கண்டு, 'பசி என்னும் நோயைத் தீர்க்கும் மருத்துவனான பண்ணனின் இல்லம் அருகில் உள்ளதா அல்லது தொலைவில் உள்ளதா? எங்களுக்குச் சொல்லுங்கள்!' என்று மீண்டும் மீண்டும் தெளிவாகக் கேட்கிறோம்.","explanation":"The poet, Chola king Kiḷḷivaḷavaṉ, praises the extraordinary generosity of Paṇṇaṉ, the chief of Ciṟukuṭi. He begins with a grand wish that his own royal lifespan be added to Paṇṇaṉ's life, as Paṇṇaṉ's survival is vital for the poor. The poet describes the lively atmosphere around Paṇṇaṉ's home, where the sound of feasting is as loud as birds chirping on a ripe fruit tree. He uses a vivid simile comparing poor children walking away with hands full of rice to tiny ants carrying eggs to high ground before a rainstorm. By calling Paṇṇaṉ the 'doctor who cures the disease of hunger' (pacippiṇi maruttuvaṉ), the poet elevates charity to a life-saving medical act.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.2],[1.2,1.3],[1.3,1.7],[1.7,3.0],[3.0,3.1],[3.1,3.4],[3.4,4.2],[4.2,4.6],[4.6,5.6],[5.6,5.8],[5.87,6.5],[6.5,8.15],[8.15,8.15],[8.15,8.2],[8.2,8.6],[8.6,8.9],[8.9,9.9],[9.9,10.3],[10.3,10.8],[10.8,11.2],[11.2,12.1],[